 ],
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "tri",
   "title": "A right-angled triangle",
   "narration": "Look at **ΔABC**. The corner at **C** is a perfect square corner — exactly **90°**. A triangle with a 90° corner is called a **right-angled triangle**, and here **∠C = 90°**.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "sq": 0,
      "hl": 0,
      "askC": 0,
      "a": 4,
      "b": 3
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "sideA",
   "title": "Side a = BC",
   "narration": "The side **BC** is opposite **∠A**. Its length is written **a**. In this triangle  [[legA|a = BC = {{a|1}}]].",
   "actions": [
    {
     "pulse": "sideA",
     "at": 900
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "sideB",
   "title": "Side b = AC",
   "narration": "The side **AC** is opposite **∠B**. Its length is written **b**. In this triangle  [[legB|b = AC = {{b|1}}]].",
   "actions": [
    {
     "pulse": "sideB",
     "at": 900
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "sideC",
   "title": "The hypotenuse c = AB",
   "narration": "The side **AB** faces the right angle (it is opposite **∠C**). It is the [[hyp|hypotenuse]], written **c**, and it is always the **longest** side. Here  [[hyp|c = AB = {{c|2}}]].",
   "actions": [
    {
     "pulse": "sideC",
     "at": 900
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "squares",
   "title": "A square on every side",
   "narration": "Build a square on each side. A square with side s has area **s × s**. The square on [[legA|BC]] has area {{a|1}} × {{a|1}} = [[legA|{{a^2|2}}]], the square on [[legB|AC]] has area [[legB|{{b^2|2}}]], and the square on the [[hyp|hypotenuse AB]] has area [[hyp|{{c^2|2}}]].",
   "actions": [
    {
     "tween": {
      "sq": 1
     },
     "dur": 1000
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "count",
   "title": "Count the little squares",
   "narration": "Cut each square into **1 × 1** little squares. The two smaller squares hold [[legA|{{a^2|2}}]] + [[legB|{{b^2|2}}]] = **{{a^2+b^2|2}}** little squares — and the big [[hyp|hypotenuse square]] holds **{{c^2|2}}**. They are exactly equal!",
   "actions": [
    {
     "pulse": [
      "sqA",
      "sqB"
     ],
     "at": 1100
    },
    {
     "pulse": "sqC",
     "at": 1800
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "theorem",
   "title": "Pythagoras' Theorem",
   "narration": "This is true in **every** right-angled triangle. In ΔABC, if **∠C = 90°**, then \\(\\role{hyp}{AB^2} = \\role{legA}{BC^2} + \\role{legB}{AC^2}\\), that is \\[ \\role{hyp}{c^2} = \\role{legA}{a^2} + \\role{legB}{b^2} \\]The square on the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares on the other two sides.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "pulse": "sqC",
     "at": 300
    },
    {
     "pulse": [
      "sqA",
      "sqB"
     ],
     "at": 1000
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "drag",
   "title": "Now you change it!",
   "narration": "Drag the two dots on the triangle — or use the sliders. Watch it stretch: now **a = {{a|1}}**, **b = {{b|1}}** and **c = {{c|2}}**. The squares change, yet  {{a^2|2}} + {{b^2|2}} = {{c^2|2}}  stays true!",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "hl": 1
     }
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "a": 8,
      "b": 6
     },
     "at": 300,
     "dur": 2200
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "use",
   "title": "Use it to find a side",
   "narration": "Know two sides? You can find the third! Add the squares, then take the square root:  \\(c = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\\).  With a = {{a|1}} and b = {{b|1}}:  c = √({{a^2|2}} + {{b^2|2}}) = √{{a^2+b^2|2}} = **{{c|2}}**.  Try the challenges — then play freely!",
   "actions": [],
   "challenge": "find_c"
  }
 ],
 "formulas": [
  {
   "title": "Pythagoras' Theorem",
   "tex": "\\role{hyp}{c^2} = \\role{legA}{a^2} + \\role{legB}{b^2}",
   "filled": "\\role{hyp}{ {{c^2|2}} } = \\role{legA}{ {{a^2|2}} } + \\role{legB}{ {{b^2|2}} }",
   "text": "In ΔABC with ∠C = 90°:  AB² = BC² + AC². The square on the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares on the other two sides."
  },
  {
   "title": "Finding the hypotenuse  c = AB",
   "tex": "\\role{hyp}{c} = \\sqrt{\\role{legA}{a^2} + \\role{legB}{b^2}}",
   "filled": "\\role{hyp}{ {{c|2}} } = \\sqrt{ {{a^2|2}} + {{b^2|2}} } = \\sqrt{ {{a^2+b^2|2}} }",
   "text": "Add the two squares, then take the square root."
  },
  {
   "title": "Finding the side  b = AC",
   "tex": "\\role{legB}{b} = \\sqrt{\\role{hyp}{c^2} - \\role{legA}{a^2}}",
   "filled": "\\role{legB}{ {{b|2}} } = \\sqrt{ {{c^2|2}} - {{a^2|2}} } = \\sqrt{ {{c^2-a^2|2}} }",
   "text": "Looking for a shorter side? Subtract the other shorter side's square from the hypotenuse's square."
  },
